# Secrets. These patterns are deliberately overlapping and deliberately
# unanchored: rule-110-arcade leaked live private keys because a /data/-only
# rule did not match a directory someone had named data-sqlite-backup/.
# Any key that has ever existed in this repository must be treated as burned.
/data/
data/
data-*/
*-backup/
*.key
keys.json
*.env

# Tag secrets, in every form they take. The previous rule here was the bare
# word `secrets.csv`, which matches a file called exactly that and nothing
# else -- so `B20260901-AD87F5.secrets.csv`, which is what the export command
# actually writes, was not covered. Each line of one of those files can redeem
# a tag. So can each QR code on a printed sheet.
*secrets*
*.secrets.*
/run-ttn/

# Signed application binaries. Large, rebuildable, and not source.
*.apk
*.aab
*.ipa

# Databases
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-shm
*.sqlite-wal

# Build output
/wildtag
/spike
*.log
*.log.prev

# The field app's dependencies and native build output. package-lock.json is
# committed: the storage provider is a copy that tracks an abstract base class
# in @bsv/wallet-toolbox-mobile, so a floating version is a wallet that stops
# compiling for reasons nobody changed.
apps/field/node_modules/
apps/field/.expo/
apps/field/android/
apps/field/ios/

# Editor and IDE state
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store
